// Chapter 3 — the relic and the endings. Shows faction gates, triggers (guild-wary in story.yaml),
// conditional diverts and several endings.

=== temple.altar
@title The Altar

At the heart of the temple, on an altar worn smooth by centuries of nothing, lies the **Relic of Ysh**: a
disc of pale gold, warm as skin.

> guide: {player:first-name}. Whatever you do next, the guild will hear about it.

* [Take the relic] { give player relic; player:xp += 100 } -> ending.return
* [Leave it where it lies] -> ending.return

=== ending.return
@title The Return

The walk back to camp is quiet. Tomas keeps glancing at your pack.

{if player has relic}
* [Hand the relic to the guild] (requires: faction:explorers-guild >= neutral) { take player relic; faction:explorers-guild += 20 } -> ending.guild
* [Keep it for yourself] { faction:explorers-guild -= 30 } -> ending.keep
{/if}

-> ending.empty-handed

=== ending.guild
@title Honoured

The {faction:explorers-guild.name} hangs {player:last-name#possessive} portrait in the great hall, a little
crooked. Your standing with them is now *{faction:explorers-guild.tier#lower}*.
{if player has idol}
Nobody asks about the obsidian idol on your desk.
{/if}
-> END

=== ending.keep
@title The Keeper

You keep the relic. It keeps you, too: you sleep less, and dream of a door with a closed eye.
{if flag:guild-wary}
The guild's letters stop coming. Then the guild's people start coming instead.
{/if}
-> END

=== ending.empty-handed
@title Empty-Handed

You return with nothing but {player:pronoun.possessive} notes and a story nobody at the guild quite
believes. Tomas, at least, buys you a drink.
-> END
